    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0346" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v01/pg314"/>

                <head>150. Memorandum From the Director of the Office of Philippine and Southeast
                    Asian Affairs (Young) to the
                        Secretary of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d150-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                        1955</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Message from Chief of Vietnamese Military Intelligence to the U.S.</item>
                </list>
                <p>The following is a message received … from the Chief of Prime Minister Diem’s Military Intelligence with the request
                    that it be transmitted to highest American authorities. The receiving agency
                    comments that the message should properly be read as an informal but attempted
                    communication between the Government of Viet-Nam and the Government of the
                    United States.</p>
                <pb facs="0347" n="315" xml:id="pg315"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Decision has been taken to destroy all rebels supported by the
                        French.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In the event that under French pressure Bao
                            Dai dismisses Diem
                        overtly, then present government will take to <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >maquis</hi> in the name of the Revolution against Bao Dai and France.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Meanwhile President this morning sent telegram to Bao Dai seeking pretexts not to proceed to
                        Cannes (i.e. President and General Ty).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d150-f2"/> Same time Binh Xuyen
                        being defeated quickly as possible.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>President Ngo Dinh Diem requests
                        support and moral pressure on Bao Dai
                        and French to bring about postponement execution of Bao Dai’s previous decisions taken in recent
                        telegrams.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d150-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d150-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 751K.00/4–2955. Top Secret. Drafted
                    by Hoey. Also sent to Hoover, Murphy, MacArthur, Merchant, and Sebald.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d150-f2" n="2" xml:id="d150-f2-content">
                <p>As reported in telegram 4928 from Saigon, April 29, Bao Dai ordered Diem and
                    Chief of General Staff Ty to Cannes for
                    consultations. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, 751G.00/4–2955)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
